<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60052" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κροαίνω</span></b> , only pres.
		part., of a horse, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stamp, strike with the hoof</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θείῃ πεδίοιο κροαίνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.507
				</span></i>
			 (where Sch.A rejects the expl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιθυμῶν</span>, quoting <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				176
			</span></i>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρυαίνω</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; κροαίνοντες πεδίοισι</span>
			(v.l. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίοιο</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.279
			</span></i>: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				1.30
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>luxuriate, wanton</i>, of a rhetorician,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>VS</u>
				1.25.7
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλήκτρῳ λιγυρὸν μέλος κ.</span>”
				<i>striking,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anacreont.
					58.6
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
